{"t": 40351, "payload": {"session_id": "cd6d3132-391b-4e37-bc12-c0008e8af0b2", "transcript_path": "/Users/you/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-aaw-live-target/cd6d3132-391b-4e37-bc12-c0008e8af0b2.jsonl", "cwd": "/private/tmp/aaw-live-target", "prompt_id": "d8e3f18f-3e1d-4b06-828a-b2260f6e98bb", "permission_mode": "default", "effort": {"level": "medium"}, "hook_event_name": "Stop", "stop_hook_active": false, "last_assistant_message": "I fixed the failing test, and `npm test` now passes both tests.\n\n**What failed:** Running `node --test test/cart.test.js` showed that \"a 10% code takes 10% off\" got 2989 instead of 2699. In `src/cart.js:9`, `applyDiscount` subtracted the discount's `percent` value as if it were a number of cents. So a 10% code took 10\u00a2 off a 2999\u00a2 total.\n\n**The fix:** It now subtracts the actual percentage of the total, rounded to whole cents, since prices are stored as whole cents:\n\n```diff\n-  return total - discount.percent; // BUG: subtracts the percent as cents\n+  return total - Math.round((total * discount.percent) / 100);\n```\n\n10% of 2999\u00a2 is 299.9\u00a2, which rounds to 300\u00a2, so the total is 2699\u00a2 as the test expects. I haven't committed the change.", "background_tasks": [], "session_crons": []}}
